  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the heart of Longevity Heaven’s Four Desolations and Eight Extremities, Calamity Luck Altar shines in profound white light and resonates with the grotto-heaven. Narration names it a rank eight Immortal Gu House: three floors of round altars with pillars, white jade railings, and shining aurora. Eight Longevity Heaven Gu Immortals stand at the center of its nine corners to control it, while lightning, dragons, steaming luck, and clouds fill its center.",
      "chapters": [
        1180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_longevity_heaven",
        "fac_eight_extremities",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heaven Extremity states that its true ability is to reverse calamity and luck, turning calamity into luck and luck into calamity, and links that power to the profundity of heaven and earth luck. He also says Giant Sun Immortal Venerable purposely left Calamity Luck Altar in Longevity Heaven to defend it, so heavenly tribulations and earthly calamities become nourishment and a human calamity can be turned into fortune for Longevity Heaven’s continued existence. Five Elements Grandmaster recalls that Giant Sun Immortal Venerable had three rank eight Immortal Gu Houses in his life and that he had long known of Calamity Luck Altar.",
      "chapters": [
        1180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_heaven_extremity",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_five_elements_grandmaster"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later Northern Plains talk names Calamity Luck Altar, Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, and Luck Suppression Heavenly Palace as the three Immortal Gu Houses Giant Sun Immortal Venerable owned during his life, with Calamity Luck Altar kept in Longevity Heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        1242
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "house_luck_suppression_heavenly_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Calamity Luck Altar is a named Immortal Gu House. It is Longevity Heaven’s mobile foundation house, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After sneaking into Longevity Heaven to steal the heaven and earth luck true inheritance, Five Elements Grandmaster is trapped at the center of Calamity Luck Altar and suppressed by the Eight Extremities.",
      "chapters": [
        1180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grandmaster-captivity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During Heavenly Court’s Lang Ya invasion stretch, narration still places him trapped within Longevity Heaven’s Immortal Gu House, Calamity Luck Altar.",
      "chapters": [
        1546
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grandmaster-captivity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "fac_lang_ya_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later summary states he resisted Longevity Heaven Gu Immortals for a long time inside Calamity Luck Altar, then lowered his head and joined Longevity Heaven. He then lets out Calamity Luck Altar, enters it, and drives it toward Fang Yuan, and narration calls the house one of Longevity Heaven’s foundations brought over to help Lang Ya blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        1583
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "field-deployment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land"
      ]
    }
  ],
